**TRACK: Wonderland (Wonderwall)**
key: G | tempo: 87 | swing: 0% | subdivision: 8th

[intro]
Chords: Em7 | G | Dsus4 | A7sus4
Melody: (none)
Lyrics: (none)
@player guitar: strum pattern: down, down-up, up-down-up (repeat per chord)
@player bass: root notes: E, G, D, A (half notes)

[verse1]
Chords: Em7 | G | Dsus4 | A7sus4 (x2)
Melody: (vocal line, simplified, 8th feel)
Lyrics:
Today is gonna be the day that they're gonna throw it back to you
By now you should've somehow realized what you gotta do
I don't believe that anybody feels the way I do about you now
@player guitar: strum pattern: down, down-up, up-down-up (continue)
@player bass: root notes: E, G, D, A (half notes)

[pre-chorus]
Chords: Cadd9 | Dsus4 | Em7 | G (x2)
Melody: (vocal line, ascending)
Lyrics:
And all the roads we have to walk are winding
And all the lights that lead us there are blinding
There are many things that I would like to say to you but I don't know how
@player guitar: strum pattern: down, down-up, up-down-up (add accent on 2nd beat)
@player bass: root notes: C, D, E, G (quarter notes)

[chorus]
Chords: Cadd9 | Em7 | G | Dsus4 (x2)
Melody: (vocal line, higher register)
Lyrics:
Because maybe, you're gonna be the one that saves me
And after all, you're my wonderwall
@player guitar: strum pattern: down, down-up, up-down-up (full, open chords)
@player bass: root notes: C, E, G, D (half notes, add passing D-C#-C on last repeat)

[verse2]
Chords: Em7 | G | Dsus4 | A7sus4 (x2)
Melody: (vocal line, similar to verse1)
Lyrics:
Today was gonna be the day but they'll never throw it back to you
By now you should've somehow realized what you're not to do
I don't believe that anybody feels the way I do about you now
@player guitar: strum pattern: down, down-up, up-down-up (continue)
@player bass: root notes: E, G, D, A (half notes)

[outro]
Chords: Em7 | G | Dsus4 | A7sus4 (repeat, fade)
Melody: (hummed or "na na na")
Lyrics: (none)
@player guitar: strum pattern: down, down-up, up-down-up (gradually lighter)
@player bass: root notes: E, G, D, A (whole notes, fade)
